SUMMARY:Lower Strength + Knee Capacity
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3500 kcal\, 180 g protein\, 505 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protei
 n in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again af
 ter.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for sched
 ule constraints.\n- Adjusted for temporary low-back recovery constraint.\
 n\nWarm-Up:\n- 7-8 min bike\, ankle rocks\, bodyweight squats\, and short
 -foot activation.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: double progression\; add 
 load only when knee tracking stays clean\, discomfort stays 0-2/10\, and 
 top sets stay near RPE 6-7. Temporary low-back recovery constraint: cap l
 oaded work at RPE 6-7 and stop if symptoms rise.\n- Controlled hack squat
  or goblet squat: 3 x 6-10 at RPE 6-7\; stop if symptoms rise.\n- Back-fr
 iendly posterior chain: seated or lying leg curl 3 x 10-15 at RPE 6-7\, p
 lus bodyweight glute bridge 2 x 12 if symptom-free.\n- Leg extension: 3 x
  12-15 at RPE 6-7 paired with front-foot elevated split squat 2-3 x 8-10 
 per leg at RPE 7.\n- Core finisher: seated calf raise plus tibialis raise
 s 4 x 12-20 each at RPE 7\, then side plank 2 x 30 sec. Temporary low-bac
 k recovery constraint: avoid loaded hinging and max-brace loading\; use m
 achines or supported positions where possible.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily m
 acros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates before and aft
 er training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobilit
 y if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
