SUMMARY:Upper Calisthenics + Shoulder Hypertrophy
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 175 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 35-45 g protein in 4 meals\, 40-70 g carbs before 
 lifting\, and a protein-plus-carb meal after training.\nCategory: gym\nRu
 n volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for temporary low-back recovery 
 constraint.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 5 min easy cardio\, shoulder prep\, light cabl
 e rows\, and scap pull-ups.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: double progress
 ion\; beat total quality reps before adding load or a set\, keeping most 
 work at RPE 6-7. Temporary low-back recovery constraint: cap loaded work 
 at RPE 6-7 and stop if symptoms rise.\n- Pull-ups: 5 x 4-8 or 20-30 total
  quality reps at RPE 6-7.\n- Dips or push-ups: 3 x 8-15 at RPE 6-7 paired
  with one-arm dumbbell row or cable row 3 x 8-12 at RPE 6-7.\n- Shoulder 
 and chest block: incline dumbbell press 2-3 x 8-12 at RPE 6-7 plus pec-de
 ck 2 x 10-15\, lateral raises 3 x 15-20\, and rear delt fly 2 x 15-20.\n-
  Arm and core finisher: tricep pulldown 2 x 10-15 plus hanging leg raises
  2-3 sets at RPE 6-7. Temporary low-back recovery constraint: avoid loade
 d hinging and max-brace loading\; use machines or supported positions whe
 re possible.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\,
  and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep
  window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
