SUMMARY:Plyometrics + Hill Sprint Technique
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3600 kcal\, 170 g protein\, 550 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: 80-110 g carbs in the 2-3 hours before running\, 
 25-35 g protein after\, and another carb-heavy meal within 2 hours.\nCate
 gory: sprint\nRun volume: 3 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for schedule con
 straints.\n- Adjusted for temporary low-back recovery constraint.\n\nWarm
 -Up:\n- 10-12 min easy plus leg swings\, A-skips\, ankling\, and 3 relaxe
 d strides.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: add sprint reps only when contac
 ts stay snappy and knees stay quiet the next day\; sprint RPE 6-7\, never
  max. Temporary low-back recovery constraint: cap loaded work at RPE 6-7 
 and stop if symptoms rise.\n- Plyometrics: pogos 3 x 20 sec and snap-down
 s 3 x 5 at crisp RPE 6-7.\n- Hill sprints: 6 x 10-12 sec uphill at sprint
  RPE 6-7\; full walk-back recovery.\n- Stop the sprint set if mechanics g
 et sloppy or knees feel sharp.\n\nOptional:\n- weighted sit-ups 2 x 8-12 
 and side plank 2 x 30 sec per side. Temporary low-back recovery constrain
 t: avoid loaded hinging and max-brace loading\; use machines or supported
  positions where possible.\n\nRun:\n- Planned running volume: 3 km.\n\nFu
 eling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohy
 drates before and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:0
 0-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
