SUMMARY:Legs + Delts Accessory
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 175 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 35-45 g protein in 4 meals\, 40-70 g carbs before 
 lifting\, and a protein-plus-carb meal after training.\nCategory: gym\nRu
 n volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for schedule constraints.\n- Adj
 usted for temporary low-back recovery constraint.\n- Adjusted for recover
 y constraint.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 5-6 min easy bike\, ankle rocks\, band pull-
 aparts\, and one ramp set for each pairing.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression:
  keep this short and low-fatigue\; stop 1-2 reps before failure and leave
  fresher than you arrived. Temporary low-back recovery constraint: cap lo
 aded work at RPE 6-7 and stop if symptoms rise. Recovery constraint: avoi
 d impact\, fast push-off\, and exercises that worsen next-morning symptom
 s.\n- Leg extension: 3 x 12-18 at RPE 6-7 paired with seated or lying ham
 string curl 3 x 10-15 at RPE 6-7.\n- Ankle tendon rehab: foot-intrinsic a
 ctivation\, short-foot / arch lifts\, isometric inversion and eversion\, 
 sole-to-sole isometrics\, and banded eversion or inversion within 0-2/10 
 symptoms.\n- Rear delt fly or reverse pec-deck: 2-3 x 15-20 at RPE 6-7\; 
 if time is tight\, complete the first 3 exercises and leave.\n- Chest/bac
 k/core top-up: push-ups 2 x clean reps\, dips 2 x 6-10\, cable row 2 x 10
 -12\, face pulls 2 x 12-15\, Pallof press 3 x 10 per side\, plank variati
 ons 2 x 30-45 sec\, kettlebell side bend 2 x 10-12\, around the head kett
 lebell 2 x 8 each way\, and weighted sit-ups 2 x 8-12. Temporary low-back
  recovery constraint: avoid loaded hinging and max-brace loading\; use ma
 chines or supported positions where possible.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily ma
 cros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates before and afte
 r training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility
  if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
