SUMMARY:Lower Hypertrophy + Posterior Chain
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3500 kcal\, 180 g protein\, 505 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protei
 n in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again af
 ter.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Back-friendly load
 ing ramp.\n- Return-to-impact loading ramp.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 7-8 min bike\,
  split squat isometric holds\, ankle rocks\, and hinge ramp sets.\n\nMain
  Work:\n- Progression: double progression\; add load only when tempo and 
 knee control stay stable at RPE 8 or lower. Low-back ramp: start lightly 
 and add load only when the next morning is symptom-free. Return-to-impact
  ramp: progress only when symptoms stay 0-2/10 and the next morning is no
 t worse.\n- Bulgarian split squat or front-foot elevated split squat: 4 x
  8-10 per leg at RPE 7-8.\n- Back-friendly posterior chain: hip thrust\, 
 glute bridge\, or leg curl 3 x 8-12 at RPE 6-7\; skip loaded hinges and b
 ack-extension work\; start lightly.\n- Reverse Nordic curls: 2 x 6-10 at 
 RPE 7 paired with leg extension 2 x 15-20 at RPE 8.\n- Ankle tendon rehab
 : foot-intrinsic activation\, short-foot / arch lifts\, isometric inversi
 on and eversion\, sole-to-sole isometrics\, and banded eversion or invers
 ion within 0-2/10 symptoms.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protei
 n near target\, and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\nRec
 overy:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel st
 iff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
